    "CISCO_BULLETS": [
        "Developed Java 21 and Spring Boot 3.x lifecycle event handlers for an enterprise document management integration platform, implementing business rules for employee lifecycle events and supporting consistent document processing across recruiting, onboarding, transfers, and termination workflows.",
        "Designed a unified REST API controller to receive employee lifecycle events, validate request data, generate request identifiers, and route event types to dedicated handler components, providing a consistent interface for connected enterprise systems.",
        "Implemented a standardized API response structure containing request identifiers, employee information, processing status, and messages, together with layered validation to return actionable errors for missing or invalid event-specific fields.",
        "Developed a reusable abstract event handler to centralize mandatory field validation, idempotency checks, exception handling, audit persistence, and response generation, reducing duplicated implementation across the lifecycle event handlers.",
        "Implemented duplicate-event protection using integration event identifiers and MongoDB request logs, allowing repeated requests to be identified and handled consistently without unintentionally repeating document lifecycle operations.",
        "Integrated Box Enterprise Plus using the Box Java SDK and OAuth 2.0 Client Credentials Grant, supporting secure service-to-service communication and document operations associated with enterprise HR workflows.",
        "Developed folder management logic using MongoDB mapping collections and Box APIs, coordinating folder lookup and deletion operations while ensuring that processing outcomes reflected the actual results of document management requests.",
        "Implemented recursive folder traversal and ordered deletion utilities, processing child files and folders before parent folders to support reliable cleanup of document structures during applicable employee lifecycle events.",
        "Developed candidate rejection handling that restricted document cleanup to the applicable candidate and job requisition path, protecting unrelated requisitions and maintaining accurate folder mapping status after successful processing.",
        "Implemented no-show processing for future employees who did not begin employment as expected, updating worker status, deactivating folder tracking entries, and cancelling associated pending operations.",
        "Developed international transfer workflows that handled future-dated, same-day, and retrospective transfers, coordinating pretransfer and active folder structures while applying documented country-sensitive access rules.",
        "Implemented termination workflows that moved applicable document structures into historical partitions, handled future-dated operations through pending records, and supported rescind processing based on the documented event state.",
        "Applied soft-deactivation patterns to folder tracking and user-folder mapping records, preserving historical operational information instead of removing all records and losing useful lifecycle audit context.",
        "Implemented effective-date processing that distinguished immediate lifecycle operations from future-dated actions, creating pending operation records for scheduled processing when an event was not yet effective.",
        "Developed client identity resolution by extracting client information from OAuth 2.0 JWT tokens and mapping identifiers to registered source platforms, improving traceability of incoming integration requests.",
        "Implemented MongoDB-based audit logging with transaction-level details, execution status, timestamps, and error information, providing a structured record for investigating lifecycle processing failures and reviewing completed operations.",
        "Created and maintained Postman API test collections covering successful processing, duplicate events, validation errors, and missing employee or folder scenarios, verifying response bodies and HTTP status codes.",
        "Maintained OpenAPI specifications documenting request schemas, response structures, error codes, and field descriptions, helping connected enterprise teams understand and integrate with the lifecycle management APIs.",
        "Used GitHub Copilot, IntelliJ AI Agent, and Cisco's Circuit assistant to support codebase analysis and implementation work, reviewing generated suggestions against technical specifications and established enterprise development requirements.",
        "Used MongoDB Compass to inspect lifecycle tracking, pending operations, worker data, and request logs, validating persisted records and processing state during development and testing activities.",
        "Applied specification-driven development by using documented functional and technical requirements as the reference for implementing API contracts, folder paths, lifecycle rules, and expected processing outcomes.",
        "Collaborated with technical leads and other developers during knowledge transfer and architecture reviews, independently delivering assigned lifecycle handlers and coordinating blockers and sprint commitments.",
        "Implemented controlled exception handling with business-oriented error codes and HTTP statuses, preventing raw internal stack traces from being returned to API consumers during unsuccessful processing.",
